                <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl after:mt-3 after:block after:h-0.5 after:w-12 after:bg-primary after:content-['']">Scan it. Then change it.</h2>
                <p class="mt-6 text-lg opacity-80">The black part on the left is the original. The grey part on the right was printed from its scan. A scan captures a part exactly as it is, which makes it the starting point for customizing it: move a hole, strengthen a thin wall, add a mount, or adapt it to fit something new.</p>
                <p class="mt-4 opacity-80">For that you need CAD, so we also offer CAD conversion. We recreate your part in Solidworks and send you a <strong>STEP file</strong>. An STL describes a surface as a mesh of triangles; a STEP file holds the real geometry.</p>
                <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2">
                    <li class="flex gap-3"><svg class="mt-1 size-5 shrink-0 text-primary" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg><span>Exact surfaces and edges, not an approximation</span></li>
